    sampleAnswer: "**Direct answer :**\nI would use Data quality when the problem matches the behavior it provides: Data quality describes whether data is accurate, complete, consistent, timely, valid, and fit for its intended use. A concrete application is A duplicate customer record can distort counts and model features even if every individual field has a valid type.\n\n**Why this is asked :**\nThis tests whether you can translate the concept into an engineering decision rather than reciting its definition.\n\n**Breaking it down :**\n1. Identify the requirement.\n2. Check that Data quality provides the required behavior: Data quality describes whether data is accurate, complete, consistent, timely, valid, and fit for its intended use.\n3. Apply it in a concrete case: A duplicate customer record can distort counts and model features even if every individual field has a valid type.\n4. Reassess the choice if the workload or constraints change: Quality checks catch problems, but business owners still need to define what “correct” means.\n\n**How to structure your spoken answer :**\nStart with the requirement, then explain why Data quality fits it. I would give the concrete example and mention the main limitation so the answer shows judgment, not just tool familiarity.\n\n**Example :**\nA duplicate customer record can distort counts and model features even if every individual field has a valid type.\n\n**Real-world use case :**\nA data analysis or machine-learning workflow may use Data quality when it needs the behavior described in the question. For example, a duplicate customer record can distort counts and model features even if every individual field has a valid type. The decision should still be checked against the workload, failure modes, and operational constraints.\n\n**Common mistakes :**\n- Treating Data quality as a definition to memorize rather than a behavior to apply.\n- Ignoring the main constraint or failure mode associated with Data quality.\n- Using it without checking whether the surrounding system actually needs it.\n\n**Interview tip :**\nDescribe the requirement that led you to choose it. “I would use it because it is popular” is much weaker than explaining the actual problem.",
    detailedAnswer: "**Direct answer :**\nI would use Data quality when the problem matches the behavior it provides: Data quality describes whether data is accurate, complete, consistent, timely, valid, and fit for its intended use. A concrete application is A duplicate customer record can distort counts and model features even if every individual field has a valid type.\n\n**Why this is asked :**\nThis tests whether you can translate the concept into an engineering decision rather than reciting its definition.\n\n**Breaking it down :**\n1. Identify the requirement.\n2. Check that Data quality provides the required behavior: Data quality describes whether data is accurate, complete, consistent, timely, valid, and fit for its intended use.\n3. Apply it in a concrete case: A duplicate customer record can distort counts and model features even if every individual field has a valid type.\n4. Reassess the choice if the workload or constraints change: Quality checks catch problems, but business owners still need to define what “correct” means.\n\n**How to structure your spoken answer :**\nStart with the requirement, then explain why Data quality fits it. I would give the concrete example and mention the main limitation so the answer shows judgment, not just tool familiarity.\n\n**Example :**\nA duplicate customer record can distort counts and model features even if every individual field has a valid type.\n\n**Real-world use case :**\nA data analysis or machine-learning workflow may use Data quality when it needs the behavior described in the question. For example, a duplicate customer record can distort counts and model features even if every individual field has a valid type. The decision should still be checked against the workload, failure modes, and operational constraints.\n\n**Common mistakes :**\n- Treating Data quality as a definition to memorize rather than a behavior to apply.\n- Ignoring the main constraint or failure mode associated with Data quality.\n- Using it without checking whether the surrounding system actually needs it.\n\n**Interview tip :**\nDescribe the requirement that led you to choose it. “I would use it because it is popular” is much weaker than explaining the actual problem.",
    explanation: "How would you use Data quality in a real project? is a core DataScience interview concept. A strong answer should define the concept clearly, explain how it works, show where it is useful, and discuss practical trade-offs. The candidate should connect the explanation to a realistic engineering or business scenario and distinguish the concept from closely related alternatives.",
