    shortDescription: "Frequently asked DataScience interview question about Feature engineering.",
    sampleAnswer: "**Direct answer :**\nI would explain Feature engineering in plain language first, then give the technical detail that distinguishes it from nearby concepts. The practical anchor is: A transaction timestamp can be transformed into day-of-week and hour features when purchasing behavior varies by time.\n\n**Why this is asked :**\nThis checks whether you can communicate the concept clearly at an interview pace and adjust the depth when the interviewer asks a follow-up.\n\n**Breaking it down :**\n1. Give a one-sentence definition: Feature engineering transforms raw inputs into representations that help a model learn the target relationship.\n2. Explain one important behavior or distinction.\n3. Use the example to make it concrete: A transaction timestamp can be transformed into day-of-week and hour features when purchasing behavior varies by time.\n4. Finish with the limitation: Features can leak future information if their computation uses data unavailable at prediction time.\n\n**How to structure your spoken answer :**\nI would keep the first answer concise, then wait for the interviewer to signal whether they want internals. If they go deeper, I would expand the mechanism and trade-offs rather than repeating the definition.\n\n**Example :**\nA transaction timestamp can be transformed into day-of-week and hour features when purchasing behavior varies by time.\n\n**Real-world use case :**\nA data analysis or machine-learning workflow may use Feature engineering when it needs the behavior described in the question. For example, a transaction timestamp can be transformed into day-of-week and hour features when purchasing behavior varies by time. The decision should still be checked against the workload, failure modes, and operational constraints.\n\n**Common mistakes :**\n- Treating Feature engineering as a definition to memorize rather than a behavior to apply.\n- Ignoring the main constraint or failure mode associated with Feature engineering.\n- Using it without checking whether the surrounding system actually needs it.\n\n**Interview tip :**\nPractice saying {c} aloud in your own words. A technically correct answer is weaker if you cannot explain it without reading a script.",
